termine":"σταφυλίνη ἀγρία","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":["cucina"],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Maghrebi Arabic اِسْفَنَّرِيّة (isfannariyya), from Arabic إِسْفَنَارِيَّة (ʔisfanāriyya), from Ancient Greek σταφυλίνη ἀγρία (staphulínē agría, “wild carrot”). Cognate to Libyan Arabic سفنّاريّة (sfənnāriyya) and several Iberian languages; see Spanish zanahoria."},{"parola":"żarbun","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"shoe(s)","termine_origine":"زَرْبُون","catena":[{"codice":"ar","nome":"Arabic","termine":"زَرْبُون","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"σέρβουλα","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"servulus","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":["moda"],"via":"","testo":"From regional Arabic زَرْبُون (zarbūn), also زَرْبُول (zarbūl, “slipper, sandal, boot, stiletto”, etc., depending on dialect), from Ancient Greek σέρβουλα (sérboula, “shoe, buskin”), from Latin servulus, servula (“slave”) through some sort of figurative use. There is no relation with phonetically si"},{"parola":"żewġ","pos":"num|noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"short attributive form of tnejn (“two”)","termine_origine":"زَوْج","catena":[{"codice":"ar","nome":"Arabic","termine":"زَوْج","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"ζεῦγος","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"grc","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Arabic زَوْج (zawj, “pair”), from Ancient Greek ζεῦγος (zeûgos, “yoke”). Compare Tunisian Arabic زُوز (zūz) and Moroccan Arabic جوج (jūj)."}]}